{"title":"2011 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An <i>arithmetic sequence</i> is a sequence in which each term after the first is obtained from the previous term by adding a constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, called the common difference. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/8/da82253c979ff59a2054e49bc8a8fd70e69d62e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 5, 8, 11, 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"17\" /> are the first five terms of an arithmetic sequence with a common difference of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/e/91e7679b01e114773e2822a8fd5615ea83def33c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 3$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the last term in this sequence were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/9/d79dc7d13216568e73c831d7b8c14c1a30f7831a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$110$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, how many terms would there be in the sequence?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1a\" title=\"2011 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1a\">solution 1 of part a</a>, we can find that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /><sup>th</sup> term of the sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/7/3d7c2219ba1657b14f550e0d1370b6201c5cdb8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k} = 3k - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/4/1a46921695c68bf025e53d3c4732ded01fb10ada.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k} = 3(k - 1) + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is the number of terms in the sequence, we then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/9/229c09919e7ff70f1d0b55ca3a82dc1b757a7ab0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n} = 3n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/3/2735a1180d81e07b408027f439af76e8c928f2c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n - 1 = 110$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/7/cf7258b9ba4b4db52c5263b9f8181bac11a07c23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n = 110 + 1 = 111$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/08766c818bff5dd68dd1071506a43c01b537ef68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\frac{111}{3} = \\boxed{37}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"122\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017224800\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.017 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 48/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 435/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2150/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.517      1 2011_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%    7.517      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36983:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017224800 and revision id 285886. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}